  "notes": "West leads the ♥K against 6♠. This looks like a cross-ruff deal. South has 3 diamond tricks, the ♥A, and the ♣A outside of the trump suit. If those tricks hold up, South will have no trouble scoring all 8 trumps separately.\n\nAs only 12 tricks are needed, declarer should win the opening heart lead and cash only 2 diamond tricks before beginning the cross-ruff. There is no reason to risk playing a third round of diamonds. A defender with only 2 diamonds will be able to ruff. A trump return will now defeat the contract.\n\nAfter cashing 2 rounds of diamonds, South should cash the ♣A. The next 8 tricks can be taken by ruffing clubs high in North's hand and hearts high in South's hand.",
